# ${{APP_NAME}}

A Go HTTP server created with Code on the Go.

## Run

Tap **Run app** in the editor toolbar, then open
<http://localhost:${{PORT}}> in a browser on this device.

## Routes

| Path | Returns |
|---|---|
| `/` | an HTML landing page |
| `/api/status` | JSON: app name, ok flag, server time |

## Stopping the server

While the server runs, the toolbar button becomes **Cancel Run app**. Tap it to
stop. The server also shuts down gracefully on `SIGINT` and `SIGTERM`, finishing
in-flight requests within 5 seconds.

## Project structure

```
${{APP_NAME}}/
  go.mod          # module ${{MODULE_PATH}}
  main.go         # routes, JSON handler, graceful shutdown
  README.md
```

Only the standard library is used, so this builds and runs with no network
connection.
